  "scenes": [
    {
      "narration": "Some of the richest people on earth report shockingly small taxable incomes. And almost all of it is perfectly legal.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "hook",
          "art": "home",
          "props": [
            "coin",
            "x"
          ],
          "lines": [
            "Billionaires.",
            "Tiny incomes."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s1"
    },
    {
      "narration": "The trick is that income and wealth are two completely different things. They get paid in assets, not salary.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "truth",
          "art": "bank",
          "kicker": "the key",
          "line": "Wealth isn't income",
          "sub": "assets, not a paycheck"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s2"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Tax is mostly charged on income, the money you actually take in.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-income",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · income"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s3"
    },
    {
      "narration": "So a founder can take a one dollar salary while sitting on a billion dollars in stock.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "home",
          "big": "$1",
          "label": "salary — the money's elsewhere",
          "props": [
            "coin",
            "x"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s4"
    },
    {
      "narration": "You only owe capital gains tax when you sell. So they simply never sell.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "center",
          "art": "bank",
          "line": "Never sell",
          "props": [
            "lock",
            "coin"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s5"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Capital gains tax only hits profits you realise by actually selling.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-cgt",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · capital gains tax"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s6"
    },
    {
      "narration": "By one estimate, the true tax rate of the very richest can be around three percent.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "bank",
          "big": "~3%",
          "label": "the rich's 'true tax rate'",
          "props": [
            "chartDown",
            "coin"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s7"
    },
    {
      "narration": "All of it is tax avoidance, the legal use of the rules, not evasion.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-avoid",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · tax avoidance"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s8"
    },
    {
      "narration": "So is that system basically fair, or fundamentally broken?",
      "shots": [
        {
